		<author>
			<name>Giampiero Fiorelli</name>
		</author>
		<summary type="html">&lt;div class=&quot;K2FeedIntroText&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;It is time to post some succulent gossip. As usual, take it with a  grain of salt.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;According to the &lt;strong&gt;Mirror&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;Madonna&lt;/strong&gt; has hired a tutor to  teach her &lt;strong&gt;French&lt;/strong&gt;, the so-called language of love, besides being  the first language of her partner, dancer &lt;strong&gt;Brahim Zaibat&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&quot;&lt;strong&gt;Madonna&lt;/strong&gt; is working on her album, but she is squeezing in French lessons too,&quot; a  source is alleged to have told to the &lt;strong&gt;Mirror&lt;/strong&gt;. &quot;Her boyfriend is  impressed, he thinks it's sweet.&quot;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&quot;She's looking at  properties in &lt;strong&gt;France&lt;/strong&gt;,&quot; the source allegedly added.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We remind you that &lt;strong&gt;Madonna&lt;/strong&gt; lived in Paris for a few time before she became a super-star, while working with Patrick Hernandez, and she has always been fascinated by French and French artists. In her latest documentary, I'm Going to Tell You a Secret, &lt;strong&gt;Madonna&lt;/strong&gt; was filmed asking her daughter Lourdes to help her to learn some French lines for her show in Paris. Lola attended a French school in London and she is an astonishingly good French speaker.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;K2FeedTags&quot;&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Brahim Zaibat&lt;/li&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</summary>
